  "content": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "In our previous lessons, we learned how to build prefix sums and how they save memory when done in-place. Now, let's put this knowledge to solve a standard coding problem: **Range Sum Query**. We will compare a brute-force approach against an optimal prefix sum approach to build a deep intuition of why prefix sums are so powerful!"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "id": "the-problem-statement",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "1. The Problem Statement"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "We are given an input array of integers, and we need to answer multiple queries. Each query gives us two indices, `L` (Left) and `R` (Right), and asks us to find the sum of all elements from index `L` to `R` (inclusive)."
    },
    {
      "type": "drawing",
      "id": "range-sum-problem-drawing"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "id": "brute-force",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "2. Approach 1: Brute Force (Looping)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "In the brute force approach, for every query `(L, R)` we receive, we start a loop from index `L` up to `R`, adding the array elements one-by-one."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
